{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789863588,"nonce":"xNi8/i/idiSCYQgn5Rscs7qiOIo=","title":"A nonlocal a nested function only writes is not shared with the enclosing body","message":"Scope::finish collects a body's free names from what it reads and what its children have free; a name declared nonlocal and only assigned is neither, so the enclosing body makes no cell for it and the write lands nowhere: `def f(): t = 1; def inner(): nonlocal t; t = 2; inner(); return t` returned 1.\n\nA nonlocal name is now free in its body whether read or not.","files":null}]}